{
  "answer": "After a breach, the incident response process investigates and resolves the event, then the team focuses on preventing recurrence. Part of that follow‑up includes reviewing who has access to affected systems. Quarterly access reviews are performed by engineering managers and section leaders, checking permissions based on role and department, and any questionable access is rejected and can be restored only through a formal access request. This ensures that after an incident any excessive or inappropriate access is identified and corrected, reducing future risk.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "passage_id": 3,
      "quote": "Incident response is a key aspect of GitLab's overall security program. This guidance will provide all in scope individuals the information they need to help GitLab ensure incidents are reported, investigated and handled in such a way that minimize security events or data loss."
    },
    {
      "passage_id": 6,
      "quote": "EMs and section leadership review CustomersDot access quarterly following the access review process, based on role and department. ... When in doubt, reject: access can be restored through an access request."
    }
  ]
}

